# Core GNOME desktop.
# We deliberately depend on the `gnome-core` metapackage rather than pinning the
# individual apps: Debian moves apps in and out of the default GNOME set between
# releases (gnome-console, loupe, papers...), and gnome-core always resolves to
# the set that actually matches the shell version in this suite.
gnome-core
gdm3
gnome-control-center
gnome-tweaks
gnome-system-monitor
gnome-disk-utility
# No gnome-software: Isoko is the way software is installed on ROS, and two
# stores on one desktop is two answers to the same question.
#
# flatpak itself stays, because the management plane installs flatpak-sourced
# applications with it - but no remote is configured by default; see
# packages/ros-lockdown.
flatpak
